<title>SWEDEN: Swedish PM says Finland ERM link unaffects Sweden.</title>
<headline>Swedish PM says Finland ERM link unaffects Sweden.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's Prime Minister Goran Persson said on Monday Sweden's attitude towards Europe's Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM) and the EU's monetary union has not been influenced by Finland's weekend decision to link the markka to ERM.</p>
<p>&quot;We will not be influenced in our decision by what others do,&quot; Persson said in a Swedish radio interview.</p>
<p>Persson stressed that the decision, whether it be yes or no, must have the support of the country.</p>
<p>&quot;This will entail listening, debate and arguments to try and gain support, and if the Swedes don't want it, it won't happen,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He also pointed out that a majority in parliament, with the exception of the Moderates, was opposed to joining the Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) and with that an ERM link.</p>
<p>&quot;Every party in Sweden is against EMU and therefore ERM,&quot; Persson said.</p>
<p>-- Lena Torlegard, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1018</p>
